# MEAVO release safety

Read root `RELEASE_POLICY.md` before any release, deployment, environment, schema, or tag/package publication action. It applies to every agent, including agents using human credentials.

- **The only human gate is merging `staging` → `main`.** Everything before it is agent work and needs no further permission.
- Create `feat/`, `fix/`, or `chore/` branches from `staging`; target `staging` in PRs; squash-merge or enable auto-merge once required checks pass, without asking.
- Agents may write to verified staging resources (staging DB scripts and data, staging deployments, staging URL repair), re-pin dependencies to approved tags through `staging`, open release PRs, and run read-only production queries through the guarded helper.
- To release, list every release PR in the bundle with its scope, checks and production steps (release tag, production SQL) in one message and wait for one human yes. It covers the bundle, including re-pins to the approved tag; ask again only if `staging` gains unrelated changes. Never infer it from the original request, green CI, silence, or an agent-written message.
- Releases are this repository's `staging` → `main` PR with a merge commit. Do not replace it with a CLI/API/dashboard release. Production actions outside a release (rollback, redeploy, env/secret change, data fix) each need their own yes.
- Never push directly to `main` or `staging`, force-push/delete them, or bypass a protection. Verify actual database, storage and external-service destinations before writes; from staging, never touch records in an external system shared with production.
